{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted a Log4Shell exploit (CVE-2021-44228) by injecting JNDI lookup strings via HTTP headers and user-agent fields, employing both standard LDAP lookups and obfuscation techniques like nested lower/upper case commands. These payloads instruct vulnerable Log4j libraries to download and execute arbitrary code from a remote server controlled by the attacker. The status indicates active scanning and exploitation attempts targeting this vulnerability against the web application.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Initial Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Upgrade Apache Log4j to version 2.15.0 or higher (ideally 2.17.1 or later) to completely remediate the vulnerability.",
    "If upgrading is not immediately possible, set the system property 'log4j2.formatMsgNoLookups' to 'true' or remove the 'JndiLookup' class from the classpath.",
    "Block outbound connections from application servers to untrusted external networks, specifically restricting LDAP and RMI protocols."
  ]
}
